You bravely walk to the shrubs of lilac plants, and when you touch branches in order to move them apart, you feel something humid and sticky on your hand! The branch is entirely covered with fuzz glittering with drops of limpid liquid. You try to jerk your hand away and release it, but all in vain, the fuzz is holding it tenaciously. Other branches are trembling eagerly near you as if they were alive. You feel like a fly, trapped in a web. You need to pull yourself together and find a way out.